{"step_index":114,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T15:37:24Z","thinking":"We need to proceed with implementation. Since user approved plan, we now need to create a web interactive app (localhost) using Python. Could use FastAPI or Flask. Provide an endpoint to run simulations and return CSV perhaps downloadable. Use SQLite or JSON for persistence. We'll implement a simple FastAPI app; serve static HTML with a form to select size and run analysis; results saved as CSV and can be downloaded.\n\nWe already have modules: orders, algorithms, counter, analysis, growth, regression. Need to adjust them accordingly: use SQLite or JSON storage for orders. We'll create a `storage.py` handling SQLite with a simple table `orders` (id, client, product, quantity, status). But to keep it simple, we can generate orders on the fly; also have endpoint to retrieve stored orders.\n\nImplement `app.py` (FastAPI) that provides routes:\n\n- GET `/` returns simple HTML UI.\n- POST `/run` with JSON body containing `size` integer triggers generation of orders, runs algorithms, stores orders in SQLite (or JSON file). Returns operation counts JSON and a link to download CSV.\n- GET `/download/{filename}` to download CSV.\n\nAlso implement persistence: use SQLite file `appresso.db` in workspace.\n\nWe need to create `appresso_analysis/app.py` (or `main.py` already exists). We'll replace main script with FastAPI app. Ensure dependencies: fastapi, uvicorn, numpy, sqlalchemy (for SQLite), maybe a simple ORM.\n\nSince we can't install packages, assume they are available. We'll create code.\n\nWe need to edit existing files that were created earlier: `orders.py` currently contains a dataclass with fields. That is fine. We'll add serialization to dict for DB insertion.\n\nWe need `storage.py` to handle SQLite: create table if not exists, insert orders, retrieve.\n\nWe need to adjust `analysis.run_experiments` to accept a path for CSV and maybe also return dict.\n\nWe'll add `regression.py` with NumPy implementation.\n\nImplement `growth.py` with weeks_to_reach as earlier.\n\nNow we need to edit files. Must use `replace_file_content` tool for editing existing files. For each file we will replace entire content? We can use write_to_file with Overwrite true? The rule: write_to_file cannot write to path outside brain directory. Since we are writing to same path, we can overwrite by setting Overwrite true. The tool says: By default it errors if file exists; set Overwrite true to replace entire file contents. We can do that.\n\nWe need to create new files: `app.py`, `storage.py`, `growth.py`, `regression.py` etc. Already have some modules, but some may need updates.\n\nLet's create new `app.py` in the project folder.\n\nAlso need to adjust `analysis.py` to accept size list and write CSV.\n\nProceed with tool calls.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"FastAPI web application entry point","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"import uvicorn\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Request, Form\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, FileResponse, JSONResponse\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\n\nfrom appresso_analysis.orders import generate_orders, Order\nfrom appresso_analysis.algorithms import find_order_linear, total_products, recursive_analyze\nfrom appresso_analysis.counter import OperationCounter\nfrom appresso_analysis.analysis import run_experiments\nfrom appresso_analysis.growth import weeks_to_reach\nfrom appresso_analysis.regression import predict_sales_numpy\nfrom appresso_analysis.storage import init_db, insert_orders, get_all_orders\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nHTML = \"\"\"\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head><title>Appresso Café Analyzer</title></head>\n<body>\n<h1>Appresso Café Analyzer</h1>\n<form action=\"/run\" method=\"post\">\n  <label for=\"size\">Tamaño de la lista de pedidos:</label>\n  <select name=\"size\" id=\"size\">\n    <option value=\"10\">10</option>\n    <option value=\"100\">100</option>\n    <option value=\"1000\">1 000</option>\n    <option value=\"10000\">10 000</option>\n    <option value=\"100000\">100 000</option>\n  </select>\n  <br/><br/>\n  <button type=\"submit\">Ejecutar análisis</button>\n</form>\n</body>\n</html>\n\"\"\"\n\n@app.on_event(\"startup\")\nasync def startup_event():\n    # initialise SQLite DB (creates file if missing)\n    init_db()\n\n@app.get(\"/\", response_class=HTMLResponse)\nasync def read_root():\n    return HTML\n\n@app.post(\"/run\")\nasync def run_analysis(request: Request, size: int = Form(...)):\n    # Generate orders\n    orders = generate_orders(size)\n    # Persist to SQLite (optional, also keep in JSON for quick view)\n    insert_orders(orders)\n    # Run core algorithms and count operations\n    counter = OperationCounter()\n    target_id = orders[0].order_id if orders else 0\n    find_order_linear(orders, target_id, counter)\n    find_ops = counter.comparisons\n    counter.reset()\n    total_products(orders, counter)\n    total_ops = counter.additions\n    counter.reset()\n    recursive_analyze(orders, 0, counter)\n    rec_calls = counter.calls\n    rec_adds = counter.additions\n    # Growth model (client doubles each week, start=2)\n    growth_weeks = {target: weeks_to_reach(target, start=2, factor=2) for target in [42, 72, 120]}\n    # Simple sales prediction using NumPy linear regression on simulated daily totals\n    daily_totals = [order.total_quantity() if isinstance(order, Order) else sum(q for _, q in order[\"products\"]) for order in orders]\n    pred_2_5 = predict_sales_numpy(daily_totals, days_ahead=2.5)\n    pred_7 = predict_sales_numpy(daily_totals, days_ahead=7)\n    # Write operation counts to CSV (single row)\n    out_path = Path(\"operation_counts.csv\")\n    out_path.write_text(\n        \"size,find_comparisons,total_additions,recursive_calls,recursive_additions\\n\"\n        f\"{size},{find_ops},{total_ops},{rec_calls},{rec_adds}\\n\"\n    )\n    response = {\n        \"size\": size,\n        \"find_comparisons\": find_ops,\n        \"total_additions\": total_ops,\n        \"recursive_calls\": rec_calls,\n        \"recursive_additions\": rec_adds,\n        \"growth_weeks\": growth_weeks,\n        \"prediction_2_5_days\": pred_2_5,\n        \"prediction_7_days\": pred_7,\n        \"csv_download\": \"/download/operation_counts.csv\"\n    }\n    return JSONResponse(content=response)\n\n@app.get(\"/download/{filename}\")\nasync def download_file(filename: str):\n    file_path = Path(filename)\n    if not file_path.is_file():\n        return JSONResponse(content={\"error\": \"File not found\"}, status_code=404)\n    return FileResponse(path=file_path, filename=filename, media_type=\"text/csv\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    uvicorn.run(\"app:app\", host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=8000, reload=False)\n","Description":"Create FastAPI web app entry point","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:/Users/juan2/.gemini/antigravity/brain/23eabdbc-225e-4c28-8288-af4260aef6b7/appresso_analysis/app.py","toolAction":"Creating FastAPI web app","toolSummary":"File creation"}}]}
