tion_7_days`\n   * enlace `csv_download` para descargar `operation_counts.csv`\n\n---\n\n## Resumen rápido de comandos (elige una de las dos variantes)\n\n### Variante A – Ejecutar desde la carpeta PADRE (recomendada)\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\juan2\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\23eabdbc-225e-4c28-8288-af4260aef6b7\n.\\appresso_analysis\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\npip install -r requirements.txt\nuvicorn appresso_analysis.app:app --reload\n```\n\n### Variante B – Ejecutar desde dentro de `appresso_analysis`\n\n```powershell\ncd C:\\Users\\juan2\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\23eabdbc-225e-4c28-8288-af4260aef6b7\\appresso_analysis\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\nuvicorn app:app --reload\n```\n\nPrueba cualquiera de las dos y, cuando veas el mensaje **“Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000”**, abre el navegador y revisa la UI.  \n\n¡Dime cuál de los dos comandos funciona o si sigue apareciendo algún error, y continuaremos desde allí!","thinking":"We need to diagnose why module not found. Maybe Python path issue: running uvicorn from inside appresso_analysis folder, but still referencing appresso_analysis.app which expects package folder one level up. Actually if we cd into appresso_analysis, the package name should be just app (module). The command uvicorn appresso_analysis.app:app will try to import appresso_analysis as package, but since cwd is inside that folder, it won't find it (no parent). So we need to run from the parent directory (the brain folder) or adjust PYTHONPATH.\n\nWe have two options: run from the parent directory (brain/... folder) and keep command uvicorn appresso_analysis.app:app. Or from inside folder and use uvicorn app:app.\n\nThe user tried both? We saw they used uvicorn appresso_analysis.app:app from inside the folder leading to error. Let's advise to cd to the parent (the folder containing appresso_analysis) then run uvicorn appresso_analysis.app:app.\n\nParent path: C:\\Users\\juan2\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\23eabdbc-225e-4